## Attribution

If you use these corpora, please cite RestoreBench and, because the base networks carry
their own citation requirements, the sources below.

## Provenance of the base networks

The scenarios are derived from two published test networks, obtained through
[pandapower](https://github.com/e2nIEE/pandapower) (BSD-3-Clause, University of Kassel and
Fraunhofer IEE), which in turn sources them from
[MATPOWER](https://matpower.org/). Neither network is original to this project; both are
augmented and stressed by the pipeline in `restorebench/corpus/`, and the augmentation is
recorded in each corpus's `manifest.json`.

**IEEE 118-bus** (`dataset/ieee118/`) — the standard IEEE 118-bus test case, via
`pandapower.networks.case118`.

**PEGASE 89-bus** (`dataset/pegase89/`) — via `pandapower.networks.case89pegase`. The data
originates from the PEGASE project and is documented in:

> C. Josz, S. Fliscounakis, J. Maeght, P. Panciatici. *AC Power Flow Data in MATPOWER and
> QCQP Format: iTesla, RTE Snapshots, and PEGASE.* arXiv:1603.01533, 2016.

> S. Fliscounakis, P. Panciatici, F. Capitanescu, L. Wehenkel. *Contingency Ranking with
> Respect to Overloads in Very Large Power Systems Taking into Account Uncertainty,
> Preventive, and Corrective Actions.* IEEE Transactions on Power Systems, vol. 28, no. 4,
> pp. 4909–4917, Nov 2013.

If you redistribute the PEGASE-derived corpus, carry these citations with it.
